    "knowledge_point": "Describing Properties of the Cosine Function",
    "problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=cos⁡x?$ \n\n- The function intersects the $x$-axis at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n- The function has a minimum value at  $x=2\\pi .$\n- The function intersects the $y$-axis at $y=0.$",
    "worked_solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=cos⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933487/assets/9c77bec4ebb04668fbff5176418ed9c09143a8660879fdf523a158c5f109006c.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. At $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ the function intersects the $x$-axis.\n\n- Statement II is false. The function has a maximum at $x=2\\pi .$\n\n- Statement III is false. The function intersects the $y$-axis at $y=1.$",
